I reviewed the PR and prepared it for merge:

- rebased it twice, after #65434 and after #65443 merged; the extracted content deduplicated cleanly (the overlapping files dropped out of the diff net-zero), and both the DependencyInjection and FrameworkBundle suites are green on top of the current 8.2 tip;
- checked the resolution logic against `PriorityTaggedServiceTrait::findAndSortTaggedServices()`: the port is faithful, including the `#[AsTaggedItem]` index/priority fallbacks, the repeated-attribute splice, and the tie-breaking order. Highest priority wins on duplicate indexes, then registration order;
- the interplay with the lazy attribute gates from #65434/#65443 is covered: computed tags that land on abstract definitions are skipped by the pass, so the map only ever contains concrete classes;
- the `XmlDumper` addition is write-only debug output on 8.x (there is no XML loader anymore), and `debug:container` reloads the builder from the serialized dump, which the new argument survives as it holds only strings and arrays;
- `resolveServices()` returning the stored values before the pass has run is covered by a test and matches how `ServiceLocatorArgument` behaves, so I left it as is;
- I updated the description: the priority paragraph was stale (priority support was added on request during the review), and the doc points are now listed at the end.

Good to merge on my side once CI confirms.

Thank you @HypeMC for the feature and for keeping the extraction in sync, that made the deduplication painless.
